.TH OMACHAT-CTL 1 "2026-10-01" "OmaChat"
.SH NAME
omachat-ctl \- control the local hosted messaging daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachat-ctl
[--socket PATH] COMMAND
.SH COMMANDS
status [--json], fingerprint [--qr], send CONVERSATION TEXT,
hosted-conversations [--cursor CURSOR], hosted-history CONVERSATION [--before SEQUENCE] [--limit COUNT],
hosted-mark-read CONVERSATION SEQUENCE, hosted-open-dm HANDLE, hosted-claim-handle HANDLE,
hosted-resolve-handle HANDLE, hosted-create-workspace NAME,
hosted-create-channel WORKSPACE_ID NAME, hosted-add-member WORKSPACE_ID HANDLE.
Hosted commands accept --json. Conversations have the hosted: prefix.
.SH PANIC
panic --confirm ERASE requests and redeems a private single-use confirmation token.
It erases local credentials and history, not server messages or backups.
